            "text_HhMe9b": {
              "type": "text",
              "name": "t:names.text",
              "settings": {
                "text": "<p>For Necesito Coffee Roasters LLC, a new home roastery in Estero, Florida, coffee is an opportunity to bring neighbors together. Serving The Place at Corkscrew, a gated community along Corkscrew Road, the business is taking shape around small-batch roasting and neighborhood connections. Owners Jeff and Sydne McKechnie are excited to begin this venture and look forward to meeting their neighbors over a cup of coffee.<br/><br/>At the center of Necesito’s operation is a Mill City Roasters MCR-2E electric roaster. The manufacturer describes the 2-kilogram machine as designed for small-batch production, with digital controls and RoastPATH connectivity. For Necesito, the machine anchors the owners’ new home roasting operation.</p>",
                "width": "fit-content",
                "max_width": "normal",
                "alignment": "left",
